    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\n### Problem:  \nOpening a tag in an xml file with lemminx yelds this exception:\n```                                                                                                                                                                           \nvim.schedule callback: ...site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim.git/lua/mini/completion.lua:1973: attempt to index local 'lsp_item' (a nil value)\nstack traceback:\n        ...site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim.git/lua/mini/completion.lua:1973: in function 'normalize_item_doc'\n        ...site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim.git/lua/mini/completion.lua:1491: in function 'info_window_lines'\n        ...site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim.git/lua/mini/completion.lua:1442: in function ''\n        vim/_editor.lua: in function <vim/_editor.lua:0> \n```\n\n<img width=\"570\" height=\"342\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a4494752-8f68-4995-a1a6-8d67adf85b45\" />\n\nAnd below:  \n<img width=\"1246\" height=\"179\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f1aa642c-50e2-489d-b278-9b2c1b228925\" />\n\n### Expected behaviour:  \nNo erroring 😄 \n\n### Local fix:\n(Sure, it's hacky)\n```diff\n% git diff main                \ndiff --git a/lua/mini/completion.lua b/lua/mini/completion.lua\nindex 9e106166..524e81db 100644\n--- a/lua/mini/completion.lua\n+++ b/lua/mini/completion.lua\n@@ -1969,6 +1969,8 @@ H.map = function(mode, lhs, rhs, opts)\n end\n \n H.normalize_item_doc = function(lsp_item, fallback_info)\n+  if not lsp_item then return {} end\n+\n```\n\n### Reproduction\n\nCreating a minimal testcase is not so easy since it requires the Lemminx LSP.\n\nHaving said that, I can consistently recreate this bug on 0.11.4 and 0.12 nightly;\n\n1. git clone https://gitlab.com/kaspervdheijden/kickstart.git\n (in min.starter, hit `m` to install defined LSP's. I'm not using mason, so its basically a shellscript that installs various LSP's. Alternatively have the mason/bin dir part of the PATH)\n2. `:e test.xml`\n3. In insert mode, type `<`\n",
