        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now be resolved on latest `main`.\n\nI believe the problem here lies in the server itself: it seems to return exactly nothing in response to `completionItem/resolve` request (which is done before trying to show info window in an attempt to get more information from the server). And by \"nothing\" it looks like there is both no error and no response (i.e. both are `nil` in Lua's LSP handler). The server advertises that it is capable of performing such request (it has `completionProvider.resolveProvider = true` in its server capabilities). And I highly doubt that it is a problem on Neovim's side.\n\nWhat's more confusing is that *I think* the strict interpretation of [`completionItem/resolve` request docs](https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/specifications/lsp/3.17/specification/#completionItem_resolve) also doesn't imply that there should be either response or the error. Although, the result *should be* of type `CompletionItem` and can not be `nil` (i.e. at least server should return an item used for the request). If you are interested, I think it is worth creating an issue for the server itself.\n\nLuckily, the 'mini.completion' can accommodate this use case pretty straightforwardly. It tried to fall back to the original LSP candidate only if there was an explicit error (which is reasonable if it is an \"either...or\" situation). Changing it to try fall back to the original item regardless of the error fixes this.",
